  "rationale": "Benny Golson's second Riverside album gathers a peak hard-bop sextet: Kenny Dorham, J.J. Johnson, Wynton Kelly, Paul Chambers, and Max Roach. The program is all Golson originals (plus two Gigi Gryce contributions) and is praised by AllMusic and Penguin Guide as a defining statement of the modern mainstream circa 1957. It adds a composer-leader voice not yet represented in the canon and strengthens the mid-1950s Riverside hard-bop thread. Session gravity and discovery value are high.",
